<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="
           http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
           http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      trade_config: the intraday clock, the exact-offset strike, and the book id.

      Added for the Pressure strategy (Strategy 5, docs/PRESSURE_STRATEGY.md).
      Every column here is a trading-behaviour number under CLAUDE.md #9 - it
      decides when a trade may open, how long it may live, and which contract it
      opens on - so it is config, not a constant in a service.

      BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL FOR EVERY EXISTING CONFIG
      ===========================================
      All eight columns are nullable (or default FALSE) and every consumer treats
      null as "the rule that applied before this changeset":

        entry_from / entry_to    null -> no entry-time window, entries allowed
                                 whenever a signal fires (today's behaviour)
        max_hold_minutes         null -> no time stop; a trade exits only on
                                 target / stop / trail / end-of-day force close
        flatten_at               null -> no intraday flatten; the replay's
                                 15:20 force-close sweep remains the only one
        strike_offset_points     null -> AnalysisScheduler keeps using the
                                 itm_depth / otm_depth strike-SET expansion
        strike_step_points       null -> fall back to instrument.strike_points
        book_id                  null -> the one-position-per-book cap does not
                                 apply; only the existing per-config caps do
        underlying_leg           FALSE -> the config trades an option, as always

      So strategies 1-4 are bit-identical after this lands. That is deliberate
      and it is asserted: PressureConfigColumnsAreOptionalTest pins that a config
      with all eight unset takes exactly the pre-042 path.

      WHY strike_step_points EXISTS AT ALL
      ====================================
      instrument.strike_points is 100 for NIFTY while historical_option_candles
      is on a 50-point grid (20250, 20300, 20350 ...). Both are "correct" for
      their own consumer - the live Kite chain and the imported ICICI CSVs - and
      changing the instrument row would silently move every strike strategies 1-4
      pick on historical replay, which is a Rule 0 behaviour change needing its
      own measured before/after. Giving the config its own step lets the Pressure
      books address the real 50-point grid while the shared row stays untouched.

      WHY THE OFFSET IS SIGNED FROM ATM, NOT A DEPTH COUNT
      ====================================================
      itm_depth / otm_depth are COUNTS of strike steps and they expand into a SET
      of strikes that AbstractSmaCrossStrategy then ranks by premium. Pressure
      needs one exact contract - "ATM minus 300 points" - so the offset is in
      POINTS and resolves to a single strike:

          strike_offset_points > 0   ITM by that many points
          strike_offset_points = 0   ATM
          strike_offset_points < 0   OTM by that many points

          CE strike = ATM - strike_offset_points
          PE strike = ATM + strike_offset_points

      WHY book_id IS A STRING AND NOT A FOREIGN KEY
      =============================================
      A "book" is a comparison bucket in a measurement run (SELL_ITM300,
      BUY_ATM, SPOT ...), not a durable domain entity. What it has to do is let
      OrderService count OPEN trades across the CE config and the PE config that
      together make one book, so that "ONE position at a time" holds across both
      legs - every existing cap keys on (trade_config_id, strategy_id) and would
      otherwise let a CE short and a PE short run concurrently. A shared label is
      exactly enough for that and needs no second table.

      WHY underlying_leg IS NOT JUST trading_side = 'SPOT'
      ====================================================
      resolveOptionType() in both AnalysisScheduler and AbstractSmaCrossStrategy
      derives CE/PE from trading_side and returns null - "fetch nothing" - for
      anything else. Overloading that column would make a spot config look like a
      broken option config to two shared code paths. An explicit boolean keeps
      the branch visible at every call site.
    -->
    <changeSet id="042_add_pressure_clock_and_strike_offset" author="moneymaker">
        <!--
          Guarded exactly as 035 / 041 were, for the same reason: this project
          runs spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=update, so a branch booted with the
          entity present but this file not yet in the master lets Hibernate
          create the columns first, and a bare addColumn then dies on the next
          start with "Duplicate column name".
        -->
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <not>
                <columnExists tableName="trade_config" columnName="book_id"/>
            </not>
        </preConditions>
        <addColumn tableName="trade_config">
            <!--
              Earliest time-of-day a NEW entry may open. Inclusive. The Pressure
              spec's "first new entry after 09:25 inclusive" - it exists because
              the opening range is only complete at 09:30 and RSI/ADX are still
              warming from the previous session before that.
            -->
            <column name="entry_from" type="TIME"/>
            <!--
              Latest time-of-day a NEW entry may open. Inclusive. 14:15 for
              Pressure, which with a 90-minute max hold puts the last possible
              time-stop exit at 15:45 - past the close - so flatten_at is what
              actually bounds it.
            -->
            <column name="entry_to" type="TIME"/>
            <!--
              Maximum minutes a position may stay OPEN before PositionService
              closes it with exit_reason = TIME_STOP. Measured from entry_time.
            -->
            <column name="max_hold_minutes" type="INT"/>
            <!--
              Time-of-day at which any still-OPEN position of this config is
              closed with exit_reason = FLATTEN, regardless of P&L.

              Distinct from the replay's own end-of-day force-close (15:20 by
              default, app.market.replay-last-tick-offset-minutes) and from
              CommonRules.isMarketCloseTime (15:15, which emits a SIGNAL a
              strategy may act on). This one is a position-level rule that needs
              no strategy cooperation, because Pressure emits entries only.
            -->
            <column name="flatten_at" type="TIME"/>
            <!--
              Signed distance from ATM in INDEX POINTS - see the header. Null
              keeps the itm_depth / otm_depth strike-set expansion.
            -->
            <column name="strike_offset_points" type="INT"/>
            <!--
              The strike grid this config addresses, in index points. Null falls
              back to instrument.strike_points. See the header for why NIFTY
              needs 50 here while the instrument row says 100.
            -->
            <column name="strike_step_points" type="INT"/>
            <!--
              Comparison-bucket label shared by the configs that make up one
              book. Null disables the cross-config one-position cap.
            -->
            <column name="book_id" type="VARCHAR(32)"/>
            <!--
              TRUE = this config trades the underlying itself rather than an
              option leg. Used by the Pressure SPOT baseline book.

              Defaulted in the entity as well as here: Hibernate names every
              column in its INSERT, so a null field is written as an explicit
              NULL and a column default never fires - the trap that broke
              trade_config.source and is called out on TradeConfig.isActive.
            -->
            <column name="underlying_leg" type="BOOLEAN" defaultValueBoolean="false">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
        </addColumn>
    </changeSet>

    <!--
      Explicit backfill rather than relying on the engine to apply the DEFAULT to
      pre-existing rows - the pattern 036 and 041 established. Scoped to NULL so
      a re-run cannot overwrite a value someone has since set.
    -->
    <changeSet id="042_seed_underlying_leg_false" author="moneymaker">
        <update tableName="trade_config">
            <column name="underlying_leg" valueBoolean="false"/>
            <where>underlying_leg IS NULL</where>
        </update>
    </changeSet>

    <!--
      One index for the cross-config one-position cap. OrderService counts OPEN
      trade_order rows for a (book, strategy) pair on every candidate entry, and
      the book is resolved by joining back through trade_config, so the lookup
      "which configs are in this book" runs once per candidate signal.
    -->
    <changeSet id="042_index_trade_config_book" author="moneymaker">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <not>
                <indexExists tableName="trade_config" indexName="idx_trade_config_book"/>
            </not>
        </preConditions>
        <createIndex tableName="trade_config" indexName="idx_trade_config_book">
            <column name="book_id"/>
            <column name="trading_date"/>
        </createIndex>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
